{"author":{"id":"609bf866d4a5d716c19faf5d617b3bf3de478230d29602d72aad5aa90a80466f"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1788975788,"nonce":"JCnwfzPKKtlde2veOQfrkfdDt0c=","title":"The own-module promote path refuses on an unresolved callee and falls back to the shared module","message":"`promote_uses_own_module` sends a promotion to its own module once the shared\nmodule holds 256 bodies, but an own-module promotion is refused whenever a callee\nhas no symbol in that module yet, and the refusal fell back to the shared module\nfor ANY function. There the middle end re-runs over every body and MCJIT re-emits\nall of them.\n\nMitigated: the shared path now admits only a High ceiling (`ASH_SHARED_PROMOTE`,\ndefault `high`), and a decline latches so the broker stops re-proposing.\n\nThe better fix, still open: make the own-module path not refuse -- bind the\ncallee as an external declaration the way the shared module does, or emit a\nstub-bridge call -- so the cheap path takes what it can and the shared module\nstops being a fallback. Low ceilings could then tier up in milliseconds instead\nof never.","files":null}]}